  "force_reason": "Groups are book_quote, not market_state+book_flow: the 7 depth columns cannot exist before 2026-08-25 because the venue serves no historical order book, and under --complete-cases they pin training to the live era; the 4 quote columns are recoverable to 2025-12-10 from the venue's own candles. Standing operator policy, 2026-10-21: the Sunday retrain ALWAYS installs, so the model keeps absorbing new data. The gates are advisory and the operator reads them; they are not a blocker. Quote sources are Kalshi-only for price VALIDITY rather than measured skill - the Predexon backfill is unbiased but 54x noisier, stamped a minute late, and quantises the deci-cent tail grid to whole cents in ~27% of rows, so a model trained to beat it may not transfer to a book we can trade. It scores worse on the gates and that is accepted. --peer-quote-sources all keeps Polymarket intact: the source filter matches on the bare name and would otherwise discard the gamma backfill, which is a different pipeline, taking every cross_venue row with it.",
